<title>USA: NY bank borrowings about $18 mln/day in Jan 15 wk.</title>
<headline>NY bank borrowings about $18 mln/day in Jan 15 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fewer than half of the six major New York City banks borrowed $18 million a day on average from the Federal Reserve's discount window, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>All of the borrowings were done in the second week of the maintenance period and took place Wednesday night.</p>
<p>It was the end of the two-week bank maintenance period.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
